<Base title="About — Ming Ma" description="Ming Ma's background: 15 years building products at Facebook, ByteDance, Scroll, Tranchess and more.">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    I enjoyed building products before I even knew "product manager" was a job. Through roles in engineering,
    business analysis, and data science at <strong>Accenture</strong>, <strong>IBM</strong>, and <strong>Facebook</strong>,
    I kept looking for ways to have more say in what we built. That eventually led me to a PM role at Facebook,
    and I've stayed in product ever since.
  </p>

  <p>
    Looking back, I was always drawn to projects where a lot was still undecided. From Facebook to
    <strong>ByteDance</strong>, then <strong>Run The World</strong>, I kept moving toward earlier-stage work.
    That also led me into crypto at <a href="https://tranchess.com" target="_blank">Tranchess</a>
    and <a href="https://scroll.io" target="_blank">Scroll</a>, where the industry itself was still taking shape.
  </p>

  <p>
    Want to build something together? <a href="mailto:mamingming@gmail.com">Say hi</a>.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <h2>Cool projects in the past</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Facebook:</strong> Helped the team learn what it takes to build for China through
      <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2017/08/11/technology/facebook-china-moments-colorful-balloons.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Colorful Balloons</a>, a photo-sharing app.</li>
    <li><strong>ByteDance:</strong> Was the PM behind
      <a href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/yolarobert1/2020/04/09/former-gm-of-tiktok-launches-a-virtual-ecosystem-for-beauty-lovers/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cherie</a>, a beauty community app we built while exploring products beyond TikTok.</li>
    <li><strong>Tranchess:</strong> Helped build a decentralized asset management app as a core contributor.
      It reached <a href="https://defillama.com/protocol/tranchess" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">over $1.8 billion in total value locked</a> at its peak.</li>
    <li><strong>Scroll:</strong> As Head of Product, program-managed the
